<title>UK: Novorossiisk berth reopens but tanker queue grows.</title>
<headline>Novorossiisk berth reopens but tanker queue grows.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Berth number one at Russia's Black Sea oil port of Novorossiisk reopened early Tuesday after a 24-hour closure due to heavy swell, shipping sources said.</p>
<p>The berth, the only one at Novorossiisk which can accommodate large crude oil tankers of between 100,000 and 140,000 tonnes, reopened at 0715 (local time), the sources said.</p>
<p>Loadings were being delayed by up to six days with 12 tankers including five million-barrel vessels waiting at anchor outside the port.</p>
<p>Berth number one is scheduled to close for two weeks on December 9 for maintenance work.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7930</p>
